# HTTP response tokens for Boost.Beast http::response_parser fuzzing.
# Status line, response headers, and chunked-transfer tokens incl. chunk EXTENSIONS (the harness
# wires an on_chunk_header callback that parses extensions via http::chunk_extensions::parse).
# libFuzzer dict format: CR/LF are written as \x0d\x0a (no \r/\n shorthand).
"HTTP/1.0 "
"HTTP/1.1 "
"200 OK"
"204 No Content"
"301 Moved Permanently"
"304 Not Modified"
"404 Not Found"
"500 Internal Server Error"
"\x0d\x0a"
"\x0d\x0a\x0d\x0a"
"Content-Length: "
"Transfer-Encoding: "
"chunked"
"Content-Type: "
"Connection: "
"keep-alive"
"close"
"Server: "
"Date: "
"Content-Encoding: "
"gzip"
"0\x0d\x0a\x0d\x0a"
"5\x0d\x0a"
";"
"="
"\""
